title: Game_Start
---
Jennifer: A plot of land in a foreign country and some dirt cheap labor. That's all any executive needs to make a fortune. You ready to get started?
-> I was born ready. (skip tutorial)
    <<jump Intro_Milestones>>
-> What am I doing again? (tutorial)
    <<jump Tutorial>>
===
title: Intro_Milestones
---
Jennifer: That's what I like to hear!
Jennifer: There will be three milestones to profitability. First one is due in five days, *one million*. That's in profit, you hear? Bottom line. None of this wish-washy "healthcare for the drones" crap. That'll eat into the margin. Stomp that out.
->  I'll stomp on anyone you tell me to, beautiful.
    <<set $corporate += 1>>
    Jennifer: Try not to drool, it's unbecoming. But hit every milestones and you can drool as much as you want.
    <<jump Day_One_Start>>
-> Can't we give them just a *little* healthcare?
    <<set $workers += 1>>
    Jennifer: Are you insane?! Next thing you know they're asking for time off! Then where would our productivity metrics be? #scolding
    <<jump Day_One_Start>>
===
title: Tutorial
---
Jennifer: Christ, didn't they teach you *anything* at graduate school? #scolding
<<lock_all>>
Jennifer: Fine. Pay attention, because I bill by the hour.
Jennifer: First, get your bearings. WASD moves you around, holding right click drags the map, and the scroll wheel zooms.
<<goal "Look around with WASD, right drag or the scroll wheel">>
<<wait_for_camera>>
Jennifer: Riveting. Now, see the pale dirt with the squiggles? That's dough land. Dough, right out of the ground. Product that doesn't know it's product yet.
Jennifer: Every patch only gives up one thing. Hover over the dirt if you can't tell which.
<<unlock "Honey">>
Jennifer: Honey's your miner, and you've got three of her. Click her on the toolbar or press 2, then click to plunk her down on the dough.
Jennifer: Wherever her arrow points is where the goods come out. Right click or R turns her before you put her down.
<<goal "Put Honey on the dough land">>
<<wait_for_build "Honey" 1>>
Jennifer: Look at her go. Dirt cheap labor. *Literally*.
<<unlock "Conveyor Belt">>
Jennifer: Now she needs somewhere to put it. Belts are 1 on the toolbar. Hold left click and drag to lay a whole line out of her front. #scolding
Jennifer: Put one down wrong? Plunk the right one on top of it, or hold X and sweep to pick things back up. Q or Escape puts down whatever you're holding.
<<goal "Lay a few conveyor belts out of Honey's front">>
<<wait_for_build "Conveyor Belt" 3>>
<<unlock "Dessert Stall">>
Jennifer: Dough doesn't sell itself. Well, it does, but only at a stall. That's 5. Run the end of that belt into one.
<<goal "Run Honey's belt into a Dessert Stall">>
<<wait_for_build "Dessert Stall" 1>>
<<goal "Sell something">>
<<wait_for_sales 1>>
Jennifer: Hear that? That's the sweetest sound in the world. *Revenue*.
Jennifer: Raw dough sells for pennies, though. You want it baked, and for that you need a baker.
Jennifer: Desserts get you stars too, raw dough doesn't. Spend them on the gacha in the corner and corporate ships you another girl. Or a new recipe for one you've got.
Jennifer: This one's on the house. Don't get used to it.
<<goal "Roll for a new girl">>
<<wait_for_pull>>
<<unlock "Mocha">>
Jennifer: Mocha. Your baker, she's 3. Dough goes in, bread comes out. Bread sells for more than dough. You see where I'm going with this.
Jennifer: Plunk her right on top of Honey's belt and she'll take its place. Mind which way she's facing.
<<goal "Put Mocha on Honey's belt, facing the stall">>
<<wait_for_build "Mocha" 1>>
Jennifer: Click her to see her recipe and what it sells for. She only holds enough for one batch, so anything she can't use backs up the belt. Don't feed her junk.
Jennifer: Every girl it goes through, the more it's worth. Combine things. Upsell.
<<unlock_all>>
Jennifer: Red Velvet does the fancy combo desserts. Ice cream and bread makes a cone, that kind of thing. She's 4, once you pull her.
Jennifer: Pulls get pricier every time. Bread earns you one star, a slice of red velvet cake earns eighteen. Do the math.
Jennifer: Congratulations, you're a manager. Any questions?
-> Nope. I think I've got it.
    <<jump Intro_Milestones>>
-> Do you do this for all the new managers?
    Jennifer: Only the ones I have money riding on. Don't make me lose it.
    <<jump Intro_Milestones>>
===
title: Day_One_Start
---
Jennifer: We're giving you a small loan and three drones to get you started. They're paid through the day, but tomorrow their wages will start eating into your revenue, so you'd better get to it. Call me if the workers revolt. Otherwise, see you in five days.
<<jump Red_Velvet_Intro>>
===
title: Red_Velvet_Intro
---
Red Velvet: Nice to meet you boss! I'm Red Velvet. I'll be in charge of...erm...the red velvet cakes.
Red Velvet: Honey digs, Mocha bakes, and I do the fancy stuff. You just tell us where the belts go!
Red Velvet: The girls and I are paid through to 5 pm, so we are ready to get to work when you are! 
-> Actually, how about you stick around until 8 pm?
    <<overtime>>
    <<set $corporate += 1>>
    Red Velvet: Well...the girls may not be happy about it, but we can do one day of overtime. Its 1.25 times our usual rate. #cringe
-> Is there anything you need?
    <<set $workers += 1>>
    Red Velvet: We'd get more done with more workers! I left a list of qualified workers on your desk.
===